5. Experiments
We empirically study the generalization behavior of deep neural networks from the Hausdorff dimension perspective. We use VGG networks [SZ15] as they perform well in practice, and their depth (the number of layers) can be controlled directly. We vary the number of layers from D = 4 to D = 19, resulting in the number of parameters d between 1.3M and 20M . We train models on the CIFAR-10 dataset [KH09] using SGD and we choose various stepsizes η, and batch sizes B. We provide full range of parameters and additional implementation details in appendix A. The code can be found in https:// github.com/umutsimsekli/Hausdorff-Dimension-and-Generalization. We assume that SGD can be well-approximated by the process (4). Hence, to bound the corresponding dimH WS to be used in theorem 3, we invoke proposition 1, which relies on the existence of a point wS around which the process behaves like a regular L ́evy process with exponent ψS. Considering the empirical observation that SGD exhibits a
